      "problem": "A mountain valley is monitoring the population of a reintroduced elk herd. The valley can sustain a maximum population of $600$ elk, but the herd is still below this limit. Since ecologists began tracking the growth, the population reached $536$ elk on month $4$ and $573$ elk on month $10.$ On what month will the population reach $590$ elk? Round your answer to the nearest integer.\n\n*Hint: You may assume that the population of elk, $P(t),$ increases at a rate that obeys an inhibited growth model, where $t$ is the time, in months.*",
